<p>International Atomic Energy Agency chief Rafael Grossi said in Seoul on Wednesday that North Korea is showing a &quot;very serious increase&quot; in its ability to produce nuclear weapons. He pointed to a sharp rise in operations at the Yongbyon reactor, more activity at the site’s reprocessing unit and light-water reactor, and signs that other facilities have also been activated. Grossi also said the IAEA had observed construction of a new facility similar to the enrichment plant at Yongbyon, which the agency believes could significantly expand the country’s uranium-enrichment capacity.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vhOWvfT_7tKgTE9TgH8Gvi4FUiYB2ntePd66vbXj3BF4ueTHW-2_OM4clFFHgWFK8CKdQwiJMvJEPsJvE036iJpazJC8Ke8DdOOx3z1xQ1rV' alt='North Korean leader Kim Jong Un visits the country’s nuclear material production base and nuclear weapons institute, at an undisclosed location in North Korea, in this photo released by North Korea’s official Korean Central News Agency on January 29, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Warhead estimate: Grossi said North Korea’s nuclear program is estimated at &quot;a few dozen warheads,&quot; while The Guardian cited outside estimates of about 50 assembled warheads.</li><li>Russia question: Asked whether Russia was helping North Korea’s nuclear development, Grossi said the IAEA had seen &quot;nothing in particular&quot; indicating such assistance.</li><li>Miniaturization debate: The Guardian said some experts remain skeptical of Pyongyang’s claims that it can miniaturize warheads for attachment to long-range ballistic missiles.</li><li>Sanctions backdrop: North Korea remains under UN sanctions over its banned weapons programs, even as Grossi described continued growth in its nuclear-production capacity.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>North Korea: Pyongyang has declared that it will never surrender its nuclear weapons, underscoring how central the arsenal is to the regime’s security thinking. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/north-korea-nuclear-weapons-capability-un-watchdog-rafael-grossi'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>South Korea’s spy agency: South Korea’s intelligence service believes North Korea operates multiple uranium-enrichment facilities, suggesting Yongbyon is only one of several sensitive sites. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991947/north-korea-boosting-ability-to-make-nuclear-arms-un-watchdog'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/north-korea-nuclear-weapons-capability-un-watchdog-rafael-grossi'>North Korea rapidly expanding nuclear weapons capability, UN watchdog warns</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/15/north-korea-boosting-ability-to-make-nuclear-arms-iaea'>North Korea boosting ability to manufacture nuclear arms, IAEA chief warns</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991947/north-korea-boosting-ability-to-make-nuclear-arms-un-watchdog'>North Korea boosting ability to make nuclear arms: UN watchdog</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3350206/un-watchdog-warns-north-korea-boosting-nuclear-weapons-capacity'>UN watchdog warns North Korea is boosting nuclear weapons capacity</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/north-korea-is-boosting-nuclear-weapons-capacity-iaea-chief/article70864157.ece'>North Korea is boosting nuclear weapons capacity: IAEA chief</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.abs-cbn.com/news/world/2026/4/15/north-korea-showing-serious-increase-in-ability-to-make-nuclear-weapons-iaea-chief-1516'>International Atomic Energy Agency director general Rafael Grossi reports increased activity at multiple nuclear facilities in North Korea, including the Nyongbyon site, indicating expanded capacity to produce nuclear weapons.</a> - abs-cbn.com</li></ul>